    "body": "@davidkna: I did some testing and found out that the issue does not occur on Ubuntu 20.04.4 LTS - it does not matter if it is installed from Windows Store or through `wsl --install -d Ubuntu-20.04`. By the way, the 22.04 LTS version is not yet listed for `wsl --list --online`, so maybe it is not yet fully tested (?). Nevertheless, for now, I have been installing it through the Windows Store.\r\n\r\nHere is a proof that starship works on WSL2 (see Ubuntu 20.04.4 LTS on the left and Ubuntu 22.04 LTS on the right):\r\n![ubuntu_20_04_and_22_04](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/30161753/165138776-7ea8028d-c141-4b5b-9e59-6cd3ea84377a.png)\r\n\r\nTherefore, I may simply stick with Ubuntu 20.04.4 LTS, and I believe that we can close this issue, since it is not specific to starship.\r\n\r\n@chipbuster: You are right, something is not okay with `gzip` (see Ubuntu 20.04.4 LTS with the latest gzip `(1.10-0ubuntu4)` on the left and Ubuntu 22.04 LTS with the latest gzip `(1.10-4ubuntu4)` on the right):\r\n![gzip_error](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/30161753/165138811-f83be501-4c9e-4c27-88b8-541af7aa9ecc.png)\r\n\r\nI have tried `sudo apt upgrade`, `sudo apt install gzip`, as well the tips from [this thread](https://github.com/microsoft/WSL/issues/4461), but nothing resolved this situation.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
